[2026-08-05T04:39:03.366Z] [master 66aa9831c] NetApp: default transport HTTPS and clarify TLS verify options Switch NetApp ONTAP client defaults to HTTPS and add explicit TLS certificate verification controls for both REST and legacy ZAPI paths. Changes include: - Default transport type in NaServer/RestNaServer constructors to HTTPS. - Introduce and plumb netapp_ssl_cert_verify through client factory and   constructors. - Keep support for netapp_ssl_cert_path as trust-anchor path and update   option help text to correctly apply to both REST and legacy ZAPI clients. - Update unit tests for default transport, verify semantics, and URL behavior. - Add release notes describing verification precedence and operator guidance   for self-signed certificate deployments. Verification precedence: * ssl_cert_verify=false -> disable certificate verification * ssl_cert_verify=true + ssl_cert_path set -> verify against provided path * ssl_cert_verify=true + no ssl_cert_path -> verify against default CA roots Related pattern: LP#2157914 (Manila analogue).
